  "body": "## Request\n\nA built-in post for Hurco mills with the WinMax control, writing **NC/ISO programs** (Hurco's ISNC dialect, the Fanuc-like one), plus a machine file for a typical 3-axis Hurco VMC. Conversational (Hurco's own format) is out of scope.\n\nA machine owner in the community runs a Hurco with **WinMax 09.01.393.30 (May 2019)**, NC/ISO programs only. WinMax simulates the full toolpath on the machine's screen, so each program can be checked at the control before it cuts, like the PathPilot Hub checks for Tormach.\n\n## Clean-room sources (only these)\n\n- Hurco's public WinMax help: the NC programming G-code table (it marks which codes are ISNC, BNC or both), NC M codes, NC part programming principles, NC parameters (support.hurco.com, WinMax Mill help, NC_Programming section).\n- Hurco's public WinMax Mill documentation PDF (704-0116-101).\n- What the owner's WinMax simulator accepts and shows.\n- Never another CAM product's Hurco post or its output.\n\n## What to decide from the docs\n\n- Program start and end words, program number/comment format, units (G20/G21), the safe start line.\n- Tool change (`T.. M6`) and length offset (`G43 H..`); does WinMax want a separate tool-length table call.\n- Canned cycles available in ISNC (G73, G81-G89 with G98/G99) and their word formats (Q, P dwell units).\n- Arcs (I/J/K vs R), work offsets (G54-G59 and the extended set), coolant, spindle words.\n- Anything ISNC requires that Fanuc does not, or refuses that Fanuc allows.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A built-in post `Hurco WinMax (NC)` and a machine file.\n- Goldens for contour, pocket, drill, peck, tap, two tools, two work offsets; a test that no word outside the documented ISNC set is written.\n- One short program per question checked in the owner's WinMax simulator (load without error, the sim path matches CamCraft's), recorded on this issue.\n",
